WEBVTT

00:11.240 --> 00:14.080
bringing life to the surface of the Earth.

00:14.080 --> 00:16.330
And sometimes it is a strict father,

00:16.330 --> 00:18.040
subjecting it to trials.

00:21.130 --> 00:22.880
Since the beginning,

00:22.880 --> 00:25.710
the Earth has undergone many such trials.

00:25.710 --> 00:27.260
And now they have come again.

00:33.600 --> 00:36.850
The land dries out, the oceans vanish,

00:37.730 --> 00:40.230
and vast seas of sand are born.

00:40.560 --> 00:46.730
Most life survives only under threat of extinction,

00:47.280 --> 00:51.530
clinging to the thin atmosphere that remains.

00:57.410 --> 01:02.500
Nonetheless, some struggle on,

01:02.500 --> 01:05.460
seeking out a tiny glimpse of hope...

01:05.460 --> 01:12.010
in the dry seas of sand.

01:18.180 --> 01:18.220
LEIJI MATSUMOTO'S

01:18.180 --> 01:18.220
OZMA

01:32.530 --> 01:35.410
sabaku no kouya chirabatta

01:32.530 --> 01:35.410
You looked over the desert wasteland from above

01:35.410 --> 01:38.950
kareki wo sora de mioroshita

01:35.410 --> 01:38.950
and saw dead trees scattered throughout

01:39.120 --> 01:44.500
aoi tori ga nageki naku to

01:39.120 --> 01:44.500
Blue bird, who knows no sadness

01:44.790 --> 01:47.750
machigai darake no kibou no

01:44.790 --> 01:47.750
I ground my teeth, my hope full of misconceptions

01:47.750 --> 01:52.720
okuba de kanda nigai suna hakidasenai

01:47.750 --> 01:52.720
and couldn't spit out the dreadful sand in my mouth

01:52.720 --> 01:57.220
atoaji wa namida he to toketa

01:52.720 --> 01:57.220
Left was only the salt of tears

01:57.850 --> 02:03.310
aisuru mono sae mamorenai okubyou mono ni

01:57.850 --> 02:03.310
For cowards unable to protect the ones they love

02:03.310 --> 02:09.230
michitaita asa wa konai

02:03.310 --> 02:09.230
no future waits past the dawn of day

02:09.440 --> 02:10.190
Woah

02:09.780 --> 02:10.490
oh

02:10.190 --> 02:11.030
oh!

02:10.490 --> 02:15.570
asu no tobira doko he tsuzuitemo

02:10.490 --> 02:15.570
Wherever the door to the future may lead

02:15.570 --> 02:20.580
haruka misueta me wa nidoto sorasanai

02:15.570 --> 02:20.580
I'll stay focused on what I need to do for it myself

02:20.870 --> 02:22.250
Oh,

02:21.870 --> 02:22.660
woah

02:22.160 --> 02:23.120
oh

02:22.960 --> 02:27.710
itoshiki kimi no kokoro tataku yo

02:22.960 --> 02:27.710
I will take my place in your heart

02:27.880 --> 02:36.840
itsuka tadashii sekai he kimi wo tsureteyuku kara

02:27.880 --> 02:36.840
because one day I will show you the world we should live in

02:58.070 --> 03:03.000
Episode 1: The Sand Whale

03:09.750 --> 03:10.550
What was that?

03:30.770 --> 03:31.860
Miss Maya,

03:32.440 --> 03:35.110
please don't make this difficult.

03:54.170 --> 03:56.470
What the hell's going on?

04:01.010 --> 04:03.600
Is that a Theseus Sand-borne Destroyer?

04:04.310 --> 04:05.930
But who are they chasing?

04:06.520 --> 04:07.480
A Natur?

04:07.850 --> 04:09.480
I gotta save them!

04:17.950 --> 04:20.070
Doppler radar's showing something off the bow.

04:20.070 --> 04:22.410
We've got a wide-area QTF.

04:22.700 --> 04:23.450
What?

04:23.660 --> 04:25.410
It's currently below ground,

04:25.410 --> 04:27.160
at a depth of about 100 meters.

04:27.160 --> 04:28.210
80.

04:28.210 --> 04:28.870
60.

04:29.620 --> 04:30.630
Ozma?

04:31.750 --> 04:33.500
No way... It can't be...

04:40.260 --> 04:41.340
Ozma sighted!

04:45.140 --> 04:46.350
Hard to port!

05:18.170 --> 05:19.300
Oh, crap!

06:21.030 --> 06:22.780
That was Ozma.

06:22.780 --> 06:24.240
I'm sure of it.

06:24.240 --> 06:26.490
Argh, goddamnit!

06:26.490 --> 06:28.950
That was my chance to catch it!

06:36.420 --> 06:37.750
I'm Sam.

06:37.750 --> 06:39.170
Sam Coyne.

06:39.170 --> 06:39.960
How 'bout you?

06:52.730 --> 06:54.730
My name is Maya.

06:55.140 --> 06:58.400
Um... Thank you for saving me.

06:59.570 --> 07:02.990
N-No problem. Maya, huh?

07:06.780 --> 07:08.740
Say, are you hungry?

07:09.330 --> 07:12.700
Nothin' better than some good food
to get your spirits up.

07:12.700 --> 07:14.160
Hold on tight!

07:35.980 --> 07:40.900
Port Oase

08:22.060 --> 08:24.780
Wanna go get a drink?

08:25.030 --> 08:27.400
This way, careful now...

08:28.240 --> 08:29.660
Whoa! Sorry!

08:29.860 --> 08:31.240
Watch where you're going!

08:31.240 --> 08:34.040
You drop that thing,
and the captain's really gonna let us have it!

08:35.950 --> 08:37.080
Yo, Sam!

08:37.080 --> 08:38.080
Welcome back!

08:39.670 --> 08:40.790
Sam?

08:43.340 --> 08:44.420
Who's with him?

08:49.590 --> 08:51.180
Nah, that won't work.

08:55.970 --> 08:59.560
And here's our ship's mess hall.

08:59.940 --> 09:02.350
As always, it's pretty busy...

09:02.690 --> 09:06.360
The chef here's the best in Oase.

09:07.490 --> 09:09.650
Make way, comin' through!

09:10.700 --> 09:12.530
Just sit yourself down right here.

09:13.700 --> 09:15.620
Chef, gimme two lunches!

09:16.330 --> 09:17.580
Gotcha!

09:17.580 --> 09:20.080
Two special lunches, comin' right up!

09:21.000 --> 09:23.330
Sam! Sam! Sam!

09:23.330 --> 09:25.340
Hey, just scoot on over here for a sec.

09:26.130 --> 09:27.920
Chef? What's up?

09:28.840 --> 09:33.090
Where'd you pick up
a pretty little mermaid like that?

09:33.090 --> 09:36.810
Well... It's a long story.

09:40.940 --> 09:45.980
Say no more! You can have
two sand lizard eggs. On the house!

09:45.980 --> 09:49.440
You know what they say,
it pays to be prepared!

09:53.740 --> 09:55.700
It's not like that...

10:11.340 --> 10:12.510
Hey, stop pushing!

10:12.510 --> 10:13.970
I can't see a thing.

10:13.970 --> 10:15.680
No, <i>you</i> move!

10:16.680 --> 10:19.140
What are you guys up to?

10:19.140 --> 10:20.220
Get outta the way!

10:20.220 --> 10:21.770
I can't get through!

10:22.350 --> 10:27.230
I said, get outta the way!

10:32.360 --> 10:34.700
Get your asses... outta there!

10:41.250 --> 10:42.870
The hell are you guys doing?!

10:46.880 --> 10:48.000
Hey, Sam.

10:48.500 --> 10:49.710
Mimay!

10:49.920 --> 10:52.970
Did you report to the captain?

10:52.970 --> 10:55.430
Ah... Not yet.

11:02.430 --> 11:03.350
Hey...

11:03.350 --> 11:04.190
You're hurt!

11:04.730 --> 11:06.520
You need to get this looked at!

11:17.820 --> 11:20.200
That'll do it.

11:20.200 --> 11:22.660
Um... Thank you.

11:23.700 --> 11:26.370
A scratch like that won't kill you.

11:29.420 --> 11:31.550
Want a drink?
You'll feel better in no time!

11:31.550 --> 11:33.130
Sheesh... Doctor...

11:33.460 --> 11:35.340
No... I'm...

11:42.560 --> 11:44.890
Man, that hits the spot!

11:44.890 --> 11:46.640
Oh, Doctor...

11:59.070 --> 12:00.740
You're the worst.

12:00.740 --> 12:02.950
I thought you were going out
to look for that sand whale,

12:02.950 --> 12:05.660
but instead you've been picking up chicks?!

12:05.870 --> 12:06.910
It's not like that!

12:07.580 --> 12:08.870
How is it not like that?

12:08.870 --> 12:11.670
She was being chased by a Theseus Destroyer,

12:11.840 --> 12:15.380
and then Ozma...
The sand whale appeared...

12:15.380 --> 12:16.130
And?

12:17.550 --> 12:19.340
There's something my brother
used to say all the time:

12:19.340 --> 12:23.220
"As men, we gotta stick up for people
who can't fight back on their own."

12:23.930 --> 12:27.180
As a man, I couldn't just do nothing.

12:27.520 --> 12:29.560
She's really pretty, after all.

12:29.810 --> 12:31.360
It's not like that!

12:32.400 --> 12:34.070
Hey, Captain.

12:34.070 --> 12:35.940
That Maya girl...

12:35.940 --> 12:38.240
It feels like there's more to her
than meets the eye.

12:38.240 --> 12:39.910
Can she stay here?

12:41.490 --> 12:43.370
She'll bring nothing but trouble.

12:44.580 --> 12:46.790
I-Isn't that a bit harsh?

12:52.920 --> 12:55.130
To hell with this.

12:55.460 --> 12:57.260
Wh-What are you talking about?

12:57.550 --> 13:00.130
What? I wasn't listening.

13:01.260 --> 13:03.300
Captain!

13:04.850 --> 13:05.510
Come in.

13:06.060 --> 13:07.980
Captain, it's Theseus!

13:08.180 --> 13:10.390
The military's going to try and land.

13:11.350 --> 13:14.020
I know.
The cards told me a long time ago.

13:27.160 --> 13:28.500
What're those?

13:29.000 --> 13:30.580
Military ships?

13:30.580 --> 13:31.250
Why?

13:51.520 --> 13:52.690
Halt!

14:08.910 --> 14:11.290
Your kind isn't welcome here!

14:11.580 --> 14:13.500
Damn straight! Get the hell out!

14:16.380 --> 14:17.250
Ready!

14:28.470 --> 14:31.100
What the hell do they want?

14:31.560 --> 14:34.650
You don't think they're after that woman?

14:34.650 --> 14:35.480
No way.

14:35.690 --> 14:38.440
For the military to come out this far...

14:38.440 --> 14:41.190
Sam, just who <i>is that girl?</i>

14:41.740 --> 14:43.820
I don't know what to tell you.

14:45.320 --> 14:48.330
Looks like you've brought trouble
for us once again.

14:49.120 --> 14:50.490
Sorry.

14:52.370 --> 14:53.250
Captain!

15:03.340 --> 15:05.550
That was quite the entrance.

15:09.810 --> 15:11.430
Are you the captain?

15:12.060 --> 15:14.440
We've received information

15:14.440 --> 15:17.810
that the woman we're looking
for is aboard your ship!

15:17.810 --> 15:21.190
I don't know what you're talking about.

15:21.480 --> 15:24.450
Lower the plank. That's a military order!

15:24.950 --> 15:25.860
I refuse.

15:25.860 --> 15:27.280
What?

15:27.990 --> 15:30.410
You'd sully my ship.

15:30.910 --> 15:33.160
Why, you...

15:33.870 --> 15:35.410
No one interferes with us.

15:35.790 --> 15:37.420
We bow to no one.

15:37.710 --> 15:41.170
We go where we please. That's our policy.

15:43.340 --> 15:44.800
Prepare to fire!

16:10.910 --> 16:12.410
Miss Maya!

16:15.290 --> 16:16.910
Lower your weapons.

16:17.750 --> 16:19.500
I'll come down.

16:27.550 --> 16:30.430
Are you sure about this?

16:32.640 --> 16:34.810
I'm sorry to have caused you trouble.

16:36.270 --> 16:37.680
I'm a little envious.

16:39.140 --> 16:42.310
You have wonderful companions.

16:44.900 --> 16:48.700
Stop it. You're gonna make me cry.

16:50.110 --> 16:50.950
Sam!

16:52.450 --> 16:52.950
Right!

16:53.410 --> 16:55.040
Mimay, you take care of Maya!

16:55.040 --> 16:57.330
Okay, got it!

16:58.870 --> 17:01.040
Hurry, you can get out this way!

17:03.290 --> 17:04.670
Maya, come on!

17:04.670 --> 17:05.710
Get in the ship!

17:07.170 --> 17:09.470
What? What are they doing?

17:10.430 --> 17:13.800
Captain, this is a really bad habit of yours.

17:14.470 --> 17:16.350
I guess that's just how I am.

17:17.640 --> 17:19.730
Men, we're leaving port!

17:20.440 --> 17:21.940
Roger that.

17:22.270 --> 17:24.520
Get to work, men!

17:24.570 --> 17:25.440
Aye aye!

18:08.030 --> 18:09.360
What are you doing?

18:09.360 --> 18:11.400
Fire! Open fire!

18:21.710 --> 18:22.830
H-Hold it!

18:31.260 --> 18:32.470
The Doppler radar!

18:32.470 --> 18:34.720
We're picking up something
around the sand pirate ship!

18:35.090 --> 18:35.720
What?

18:36.140 --> 18:41.480
Third-order harmonic vibration
mode detected near the target ship.

18:41.480 --> 18:42.520
How strong?

18:42.520 --> 18:43.730
200 dB.

18:43.730 --> 18:46.190
It matches the FFT curve of the QTF.

18:46.230 --> 18:47.690
They're perfectly identical.

18:48.110 --> 18:49.690
A transition field?

18:50.940 --> 18:51.860
Impossible...

18:58.490 --> 18:59.700
What is this?

18:59.700 --> 19:00.990
A sinkhole?

19:01.410 --> 19:02.540
Evacuate!

19:10.800 --> 19:13.010
Order our troops to evacuate immediately!

19:13.550 --> 19:14.970
Contact the gunners.

19:14.970 --> 19:17.970
Target the stern with turrets one and two!

19:18.430 --> 19:20.140
Are the troops evacuated?

19:20.140 --> 19:21.220
It's taking time.

19:23.100 --> 19:24.100
How's our shield?

19:24.310 --> 19:25.440
Looking good.

19:25.440 --> 19:27.310
Got the whole ship locked down.

19:27.310 --> 19:27.940
Okay.

19:28.270 --> 19:31.610
All energy to the quantum transition engine.

19:31.610 --> 19:32.940
Aye aye!

19:32.940 --> 19:36.200
Quantum transition engine output set to maximum.

19:42.540 --> 19:43.790
What is this?

19:43.790 --> 19:46.960
Did you finish analyzing the
fluctuation pattern of that Doppler shift?

19:47.330 --> 19:52.420
I'm running the survey radar's
fluctuation pattern through a dip filter.

19:52.880 --> 19:54.590
We just need to know what caused it.

19:54.590 --> 19:56.840
At least confirm the center frequency.

19:56.840 --> 19:57.630
R-Right!

19:59.340 --> 20:01.300
LS Boundary phase detected!

20:01.300 --> 20:03.270
The transition strength is crossing the threshold.

20:03.600 --> 20:06.020
LS transition has passed the threshold!

20:06.020 --> 20:07.270
Okay.

20:11.900 --> 20:14.190
Gunners, open fire.

20:15.320 --> 20:16.610
Did you hear me?

20:16.610 --> 20:17.990
Open fire!

20:26.660 --> 20:30.630
Enemy targeting laser has locked on to our stern.

20:30.960 --> 20:32.290
It's firing!

20:34.170 --> 20:35.340
Full output!

20:35.340 --> 20:36.760
Ready to launch!

20:37.220 --> 20:39.340
Bardanos, launch!

20:39.550 --> 20:40.840
Trim 45.

20:40.840 --> 20:42.220
Dive!

21:18.800 --> 21:20.180
Impossible.

21:22.180 --> 21:26.390
A Natura ship that can dive?

21:30.100 --> 21:36.480
shin'ai naru anata he

21:30.100 --> 21:36.480
I ask you, my love,

21:36.480 --> 21:43.870
since when your heart

21:42.860 --> 21:49.450
setsunasa to kodoku no aida

21:42.860 --> 21:49.450
has been lost between sorrow and solitude

21:49.450 --> 21:56.000
hasamarete kokyuu wo wasureteru

21:49.450 --> 21:56.000
where you lost your grip on reality

21:56.000 --> 22:02.470
kanashii uta ni tsutsumarete

21:56.000 --> 22:02.470
All around us we hear songs of lament

22:02.470 --> 22:08.970
namida ga ochiru sono mae ni

22:02.470 --> 22:08.970
but before I give in to the tears

22:07.970 --> 22:14.600
kizuite anata wo omoinagara

22:07.970 --> 22:14.600
I notice the echoes

22:14.600 --> 22:23.610
yasashiku hibiku utagoe ni

22:14.600 --> 22:23.610
of a gentle singing voice around me

22:23.820 --> 22:31.500
dareka wo aishite dareka ni aisare

22:23.820 --> 22:31.500
Loving someone and being loved by someone

22:30.500 --> 22:36.880
umareta imi ni sotto kizuketa nara

22:30.500 --> 22:36.880
is why we were all born

22:36.880 --> 22:44.340
omoi no mama ni koe wo furishibotte

22:36.880 --> 22:43.130
If you realized that too, put your emotions

22:42.130 --> 22:44.340
into your voice

22:44.340 --> 22:54.480
anata mo tsuyoku ai wo utatte hoshii

22:44.340 --> 22:54.480
and please sing of love with all your strength

22:59.940 --> 23:11.950
Next Episode

23:01.030 --> 23:02.070
Depth 300!

23:02.280 --> 23:03.900
The boundary phase has gone underground.

23:03.900 --> 23:06.200
I bet Theseus just got the surprise of their lives!

23:06.200 --> 23:07.950
If they don't like it,
they can come down and get us!

23:07.950 --> 23:09.160
Don't let your guard down!

23:09.160 --> 23:10.950
They know how to fight on the sand.

23:10.950 --> 23:11.620
Seriously?

23:11.620 --> 23:13.040
I can hear their engines!

23:11.950 --> 23:14.960
Episode 2: Diving Limits

23:13.040 --> 23:13.790
What?!
